          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Clover"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Actually I didn't have any honedew melon, so I made this with kiwi fruit. I doubled the broccoli and still couldn't taste it, BTW I used frozen cut broccoli - partially defrosted. Also, I had to add 1/2 C of water. Blenders need some liquid to get the process started. It was good",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-04T15:07:52.080Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "srushi4"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a very interesting idea! I didn't particularly care for it, but it was not repulsive by any means. I left out the broccoli, but otherwise followed the recipe. It's certainly refreshing; the mint helps with that as well. Not sure I should have had it for breakfast - maybe more of an afternoon snack.",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-24T18:56:38.563Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mallory Kitzmann"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The flavor was really refreshing on a hot summer day! I substituted half of the ice cubes with almond milk I did add the broccoli and added extra grapes. Defiantly going to make this one again!",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-07T10:28:10.183Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amber Stoltenburg"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed it up a bit:\nOnly 1/8 cup of Broccoli\nNo Mint (didn't have any)\nAdded a handful of baby spinach\nNext time I would only use 1/2 a cucumber, cause that's all I could taste.",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-30T07:56:10.207Z"
          },
